  "id": "rng",
  "term": "RNG",
  "definition": "RNG refers to a behavioral task in which reduced randomness in a person’s output is used as a sign that attentional control and other executive resources are under strain. It is often used in dual-task settings because higher mental demands, including rumination, tend to lower randomness and reveal limits in updating, inhibition, and shifting between tasks.",
